Local files and developer tools (@instinct-files: 0, is #chapter, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-handbook: 11) { r_12YTD2TNS4J92G5EBFZRX8ANP2
Choose a subject below. Read, practice freely or use assistance, and leave whenever you need. Earlier ideas are suggestions.
} r_12YTD2TNS4J92G5EBFZRX8ANP2

Audio, spatial and reusable tools (@instinct-creative: 0, is #chapter, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-handbook: 12) { r_4XGM5ZB8BZ7JWZVX77KXBDW6Y7
Choose a subject below. Read, practice freely or use assistance, and leave whenever you need. Earlier ideas are suggestions.
} r_4XGM5ZB8BZ7JWZVX77KXBDW6Y7

Inspecting and maintaining Lince (@instinct-maintaining: 0, is #chapter, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-handbook: 13) { r_63R30TFVCB8SP8X5QM289JHY34
Choose a subject below. Read, practice freely or use assistance, and leave whenever you need. Earlier ideas are suggestions.
} r_63R30TFVCB8SP8X5QM289JHY34

Why Lince (@learn-philosophy: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-welcome: 1, #reference @philosophy) { r_6PN5JPWVV3TWH9ZFZYY409QZQ9
A Need is something you want to meet; a Contribution is something available to help. A quantity of -1 can express a Need for one apple, 1 an available apple, and zero neither. Your running Lince is a Cell. Think of one everyday Need and one Contribution that could meet it. Reading is enough.
} r_6PN5JPWVV3TWH9ZFZYY409QZQ9

Starting Lince (@learn-installation: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-welcome: 2, #reference @installation) { r_79Z9X7PNFMHNEBS7Z8NWFQG5MY
Your Cell keeps data in its local directory and can work offline. Information shows the running version and directory. Contacting other Cells needs a connection. Practice uses separate data. Repository, container and server installation are optional reference material.
} r_79Z9X7PNFMHNEBS7Z8NWFQG5MY

Using Instinct (@instinct: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-welcome: 3) { r_2BT1WGJENZ6TC4QA00MEDZ0TRC
Find a subject through the chapter list or search. Free keeps ordinary interaction available; Assisted guides the sample action. Next performs the displayed action and waits for its result. Skip advances without it. Close or Ctrl+Shift+Escape immediately releases guidance. Start anywhere, change mode anytime and import the handbook only if you want ordinary Records of it.
} r_2BT1WGJENZ6TC4QA00MEDZ0TRC

Workspaces (@workspaces: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 1) { r_46HV3R4APT0A447VRM6A78KT8V
A workspace holds an arrangement of Sands, Castles and Areas. Select a practice workspace and switch back. A workspace changes the view, not the Organ whose data you use. An Area is a shape within a workspace.
} r_46HV3R4APT0A447VRM6A78KT8V

Canvas navigation (@canvas: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 2) { r_1XE0VM96KFSZBXTBXN903TNA02
Pan to look elsewhere, zoom to see more or less, and use Home or Fit to recover the sample view. Selection identifies your pieces. Bring Sands here moves presentations into view without changing the meaning of their Records.
} r_1XE0VM96KFSZBXTBXN903TNA02

Edit mode and the store (@edit-mode: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 3) { r_5FH4XFDNTBBBYKZNZG3GP2M7VM
Open Edit mode to add or arrange pieces. Open the store, find an item, then return to normal interaction. The store offers small Sands and composed Castles. Reveal controls when you need them.
} r_5FH4XFDNTBBBYKZNZG3GP2M7VM

Sands and placement (@sands: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 4) { r_0J3KYFP5MJS7GZV063D7RW0BW6
A Sand is a piece of the interface. Add an empty Square and a plain text Sand, then move, resize and pin a sample. Selection and removal act on presentations. Removing a presentation does not delete its Record. Ordinary Sands need no Protein.
} r_0J3KYFP5MJS7GZV063D7RW0BW6

Plain and editable text (@text-sands: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 5) { r_0VE5CQHRC6E2F1YZNREBX3KTW6
Plain text makes labels; editable text makes notes. Change a sample label and write a short note. Text size, overflow and scrolling help fit content to its place.
} r_0VE5CQHRC6E2F1YZNREBX3KTW6

Castle composition (@castles: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 6) { r_29A1SG36T8YDBHCTA82B9TDJJG
A Castle combines pieces into a useful view. Compose two sample Sands, group and ungroup them, then try an enclosing row or column layout. Fit follows content; Fill uses available space. Clipping or scrolling handles overflow. No Protein properties are needed.
} r_29A1SG36T8YDBHCTA82B9TDJJG

Appearance (@appearance: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 7) { r_6NVDCF41YXTX5BGRC4RF3QBXSM
Change one practice sample appearance and reset it. Themes set shared choices; per-kind and workspace overrides make narrower changes. Background and pattern belong to the canvas. Theme export saves appearance choices, not Records.
} r_6NVDCF41YXTX5BGRC4RF3QBXSM

Keyboard and accessible navigation (@shortcuts: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-interface: 8) { r_3NK96774SKC021JFF8529GR174
Open Shortcuts to inspect remapping. Tab through sample controls and activate a focused button. A text editor has its own input scope. Ctrl+Shift+Escape remains the tutorial recovery shortcut even when ordinary bindings change.
} r_3NK96774SKC021JFF8529GR174

Area shape and reach (@learn-areas-of-influence: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-areas: 1, #reference @areas-of-influence) { r_6RFMHMZA8JWVRDP5A2TSHTDDC7
Place a square or circle Area around an ordinary Sand. Turn it off and on. Reach controls where effects apply and can differ from the drawn boundary. Polygons are another shape choice. This first example needs no Record filter.
} r_6RFMHMZA8JWVRDP5A2TSHTDDC7

Attraction and repulsion (@area-forces: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-areas: 2) { r_5XZBWGPKMHZ791G9JQA59X3EXP
Enable practice workspace physics. Set the sample Area to attract and observe movement toward its target, then repel and observe movement away. Strength, target and simple or Newtonian choices refine the effect; start with the visible result.
} r_5XZBWGPKMHZ791G9JQA59X3EXP

Area presentation effects (@area-effects: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-areas: 3) { r_0KQFVPZK8MW2KSVT4ZWEYZ7MCS
Try one size or immunity effect on ordinary sample Sands, then disable it. Sorting and boundaries help arrange pieces. Immunity can exclude a Sand. Data-driven order belongs to Protein and comes later.
} r_0KQFVPZK8MW2KSVT4ZWEYZ7MCS

Understanding an Area effect (@area-inspection: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-areas: 4) { r_0TF0ER7ZHPTFWDJK9WPHHV081X
Inspect one cause of inclusion or exclusion: enabled state, reach, workspace physics or immunity. Use the sample to explain why a Sand responds. You do not need to open every diagnostic control.
} r_0TF0ER7ZHPTFWDJK9WPHHV081X

A Record (@learn-record: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-records: 1, #reference @record) { r_0T0TRGGAJCNQBGX00FB2HDY2DC
A Record has title, description and quantity. Edit the prepared sample and give it a slug. Negative quantity expresses a Need, positive a Contribution and zero neither. A unit says what you count. Description links connect related Records.
} r_0T0TRGGAJCNQBGX00FB2HDY2DC

Assertions and identity (@learn-assertion: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-records: 2, #reference @assertion) { r_42X48BJ3ANRH16NNB30STMSC25
Apply one concept and one relation to a prepared sample. A plain tag has no object; a relation names another Record. Main identity says what the Record is. Concepts come from a Vocabulary, so matching names can have different meanings.
} r_42X48BJ3ANRH16NNB30STMSC25

Vocabulary and Ontology (@learn-ontology: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-records: 3, #reference @ontology) { r_44TBMRPDGFRHGS1VC1XAT6EG1K
Look up a sample concept meaning and source Vocabulary, then inspect its parent and an alias. When a name is ambiguous, choose the intended source. Creating a complete Vocabulary is optional.
} r_44TBMRPDGFRHGS1VC1XAT6EG1K

Record, Assertions and Relations views (@record-castles: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-records: 4) { r_2AE13GNGXQ36QWQE7C0RAEK1J7
Open the same sample in Record, Assertions and Relations views and follow one relation. Each presents the same saved data with a different focus.
} r_2AE13GNGXQ36QWQE7C0RAEK1J7

Facts and work metadata (@facts: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-records: 5) { r_6KDD83XJXD0ZHZWRT5D9HE276E
A Fact records a confirmed change. Inspect one sample change and its current quantity. Dates, assignees, estimate and work log describe the work. A click is not proof of a saved change; wait for confirmation.
} r_6KDD83XJXD0ZHZWRT5D9HE276E

Protein (@protein: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-protein: 1) { r_04PESBG43ASBNW30QDN8KQPARV
A Protein selects live data you are allowed to see. Choose a prepared source, apply one filter and inspect results before spawning. The filter chooses data; the row template chooses presentation. Protein does not grant access to hidden data.
} r_04PESBG43ASBNW30QDN8KQPARV

Protein Castle and presentation (@protein-presentation: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-protein: 2) { r_3A4R2K8WF4PGC5CRM52W0EKWKV
Run and save a small query. Choose Title and Quantity for its sample row template. Presentation changes do not redefine the Record. Sorting, grouping, count or sum, selected fields and optional Facts are further choices.
} r_3A4R2K8WF4PGC5CRM52W0EKWKV

Areas that change Records (@area-record-actions: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-protein: 3) { r_56EMY33439N288RGJE49XVQPPF
Match only the prepared Record. Set entry Quantity 1 and exit Quantity 0, then move its Sand inside and outside and wait for each saved change. Quantity, Assertions and identity are possible properties. Inspect failure status and disable changes when needed.
} r_56EMY33439N288RGJE49XVQPPF

Protein arrangement and motion (@protein-arrangement: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-protein: 4) { r_1XS84ZBS646X60T37BJ9YKTM9Z
Inspect one sorted or grouped presentation and a destination or motion choice. These control where matching data appears. Ordinary placement and Area forces keep their meanings. Arrangement grants no additional data access.
} r_1XS84ZBS646X60T37BJ9YKTM9Z

Todo (@todo: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-work: 1) { r_6FQT1908XCGAJ5BQMTX4T2XQJ8
Complete the prepared task and undo it. Todo presents a live queue selected by a Protein. Selected-task details show its Record, quantity and history.
} r_6FQT1908XCGAJ5BQMTX4T2XQJ8

Kanban (@kanban: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-work: 2) { r_52Y0229RD50HVKHH8QTT39CT2H
Move a sample task between two columns and wait for its saved state. Columns are Areas that change task state. Counts summarise columns; assignees and dates describe the work.
} r_52Y0229RD50HVKHH8QTT39CT2H

Time Castle (@time: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-work: 3) { r_5NEE2FHN3TMQTZE4XFRZPMAC7G
Start and stop a sample timer, then inspect its work log. A standalone stopwatch measures time without a Record. A bound timer records work for its chosen Record. Decide where measured time belongs.
} r_5NEE2FHN3TMQTZE4XFRZPMAC7G

Calendar (@calendar: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-work: 4) { r_27ZXE21N3JCZ0PXW9R7N7PV06T
Find a dated practice sample and open it. Scheduled or projected changes show expected work and its source; they are not yet confirmed Facts. Frequency and Karma explain recurring work.
} r_27ZXE21N3JCZ0PXW9R7N7PV06T

Operation Sand (@operation: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-work: 5) { r_0JBH408SPEMJ29565H69R643J0
Configure a sample button to set its prepared Record quantity to zero, activate it and wait for confirmation. Commands are covered later. A button has the same permissions as its ordinary action.
} r_0JBH408SPEMJ29565H69R643J0

Notifications (@notifications: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-work: 6) { r_0PYJDFWVZCTV4SEHBTCQF89JTN
Inspect and dismiss a prepared status message. Waiting means the result is unconfirmed; success and failure explain the outcome. Dismissing feedback does not undo an action. System notification permissions are optional.
} r_0PYJDFWVZCTV4SEHBTCQF89JTN

Frequency and Cadence (@frequency: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-automation: 1) { r_5G0TYRBP3BJ34DARTYT4H17FMW
Define one sample recurring time and inspect its next occurrence. Frequency and Cadence supply the clock used by habits, Karma and Calendar. Check the timezone when a wall-clock time matters.
} r_5G0TYRBP3BJ34DARTYT4H17FMW

Karma and Rule Castle (@learn-karma: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-automation: 2, #reference @karma) { r_2W87FRQA5QP7VZ8DEC8C4MS1XW
Karma connects condition, threshold and consequence. Preview the prepared rule before enabling it in isolated practice. Inspect its resulting Fact, pause it and review history. Consequences follow ordinary permissions.
} r_2W87FRQA5QP7VZ8DEC8C4MS1XW

Daily habit helper (@habits: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-automation: 3) { r_6AQ5GAVCDTN1R91ZBK2Z6BVMS2
Preview the Record, Frequency and Rule made by the daily habit helper before importing the sample. Meet its Need once. Resolve conflicts and find Pause. Refer to Frequency and Karma for their shared ideas.
} r_6AQ5GAVCDTN1R91ZBK2Z6BVMS2

Commands and Signals (@commands: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-automation: 4) { r_5JDVBTS2F7XCVW3CEG2T2GD18V
A saved Command describes a local program and working directory. Run the bundled harmless practice example and inspect output and history. A Signal can carry its result to a rule. A Command Castle is reusable; Terminal is an interactive shell.
} r_5JDVBTS2F7XCVW3CEG2T2GD18V

Simulation Castle (@simulation: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-automation: 5) { r_21EB0V3PHR7RSVSSVHSRH8WVGE
Open a built-in scenario, step one event and inspect its timeline. Pause, Stop, replay, comparisons and checks help explore outcomes. This example does not simulate or version personal data.
} r_21EB0V3PHR7RSVSSVHSRH8WVGE

Fiote (@learn-fiote: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-automation: 6, #reference @fiote) { r_5DD8GTDQ47958MYYBQCW69J88G
Inspect provider and model settings and a prepared assistant thread containing a proposed action or question. Find Stop and authority controls. Proposals are not confirmed changes. Credentials, provider calls and activating rules are optional live use.
} r_5DD8GTDQ47958MYYBQCW69J88G

Cell and Organ (@learn-organ: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 1, #reference @organ) { r_7JC5ZH3CJSEXNCGCQQ73HQP8X4
A Cell is one running Lince. An Organ is a context for shared data and people, including your own devices. Compare prepared personal and shared contexts. They stay separate. A Protein selects an Organ; a workspace arranges views.
} r_7JC5ZH3CJSEXNCGCQQ73HQP8X4

Contacts and pairing (@contacts: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 2) { r_64HZR90VXZFPWWBDQT4KKQ5N48
Inspect a sample peer and pairing code or QR. Known, unknown and blocked describe trust choices. Proximity concerns nearby discovery. Tutorial pairing uses a prepared local peer; a real second device is optional.
} r_64HZR90VXZFPWWBDQT4KKQ5N48

Users, Roles and Access Control (@access-control: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 3) { r_64MDTKTWWVDW7EF0REBXSV51JW
Inspect a prepared user Roles and one allowed and one refused operation. Authorisation also limits visible data. Protein selects within those limits; changing a view or starting a tutorial bypasses none of them.
} r_64MDTKTWWVDW7EF0REBXSV51JW

Sharing and synchronization (@organ-sync: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 4) { r_4AB7NGB9Z1XJR33J4TX7RAV0MF
Compare a prepared shared selection with its arrival on a prepared peer. Inspect visibility, permissions and sync status. Hiding, refusal, revocation and Stop change the relationship. Practice needs no real recipient.
} r_4AB7NGB9Z1XJR33J4TX7RAV0MF

My devices and Karma authority (@devices: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 5) { r_0G3W8QZCFSE98H8ZZ0PHP22G9H
Inspect a prepared device roster and owner or execution controls. Synchronised rule definitions and permission to execute them are separate. Practice does not rotate real keys or change your devices authority.
} r_0G3W8QZCFSE98H8ZZ0PHP22G9H

Mail and delivery (@mail: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 6) { r_32W85E6XR31FW8WP2QH6DMBE5P
Inspect a prepared outgoing item and its delivery status. Mailbox storage differs from recipient receipt. Held and expired items need attention; Retry and Cancel manage delivery. Reading requires no live relay.
} r_32W85E6XR31FW8WP2QH6DMBE5P

Public Needs and Contributions (@discovery: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 7) { r_33PDKT37A1AV7KEJ31MDCTTS31
Search prepared announcements, inspect a profile and prepare a post or request. Publication and withdrawal control announcements. Subscriptions, services, block, report and moderation are further choices. A request is not a Transfer agreement.
} r_33PDKT37A1AV7KEJ31MDCTTS31

Conversations and Messages (@conversations: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 8) { r_3AE57C7E20EB1Z6514SYT8TX2X
Open a prepared conversation, send a sample Message and inspect delivery. Thread tabs, mentions, replies, attachments and requests organise communication. Practice uses prepared peers rather than real recipients.
} r_3AE57C7E20EB1Z6514SYT8TX2X

Calls and screen sharing (@calls: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-sharing: 9) { r_199ADF8E0BQB0QM90CAYGMQBVE
Locate Call, Mute, Video or Share and Leave in the prepared conversation. Reading and highlights suffice when capture devices are unavailable. Microphone, camera and screen capture are optional; Leave remains available.
} r_199ADF8E0BQB0QM90CAYGMQBVE

Transfer Castle (@learn-transfer: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-transfers: 1, #reference @transfer) { r_3A9KSK04M1686PD6A0XJBXS1B4
Inspect a simple prepared proposal, agreement and confirmed action for an exchange or donation. Promised quantities describe agreement; Facts describe changes that occurred. Prepared parties keep practice separate from real commitments.
} r_3A9KSK04M1686PD6A0XJBXS1B4

Transfers with Karma (@transfer-automation: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-transfers: 2) { r_5V6MN80TQEJJT49KP9NXXWJKZF
Inspect the prepared rule that proposes a Transfer at a threshold. Locate approvals and Pause. A proposal still needs agreement. Use the Transfer view to compare promises with confirmed changes.
} r_5V6MN80TQEJJT49KP9NXXWJKZF

Trail and handbook import (@instinct-import: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-disk: 1) { r_5G9QW9XX5EXBM5R79741W40N1Z
Preview exact handbook titles, slugs, UIDs, quantities, identities and Assertions. Conflicting identity or meaning stops import; Cancel changes nothing. Identical imports can be reused. Reading needs no import. Imported text never starts a tutorial, enables rules or runs commands.
} r_5G9QW9XX5EXBM5R79741W40N1Z

Sync and Lingua files (@learn-sync: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-disk: 2, #reference @sync) { r_7ZX4WZH37VH4FP6S9VEA2V6WBF
Connect a small Protein to a temporary practice folder. Inspect a Lingua or Markdown export and supported incoming edit. Continuous sync differs from one-time import and editing unrelated files. Inspect status and conflicts, then Stop.
} r_7ZX4WZH37VH4FP6S9VEA2V6WBF

File and blob transfers (@blob-sync: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-disk: 3) { r_214GWJFC8WFFEAWN2BG2YAB32Y
Inspect a bundled file transfer between prepared Cells. Accept, Cancel and the file list manage it. Bytes travel separately from Record text; a visible description does not prove its attachment arrived.
} r_214GWJFC8WFFEAWN2BG2YAB32Y

Storage and owner backup (@backup: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-disk: 4) { r_4PTBPFZ5532HG1Q7WEDZKV7CWR
Inspect storage and the encrypted owner-backup form. Read what it includes and excludes. Layouts, attachments and custom Castle files need separate care. History and retention are separate choices. Reading requires no shutdown, restore, replacement or deletion.
} r_4PTBPFZ5532HG1Q7WEDZKV7CWR

File Explorer and IDE (@ide: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-files: 1) { r_1Y7YWDKC4AAY8YXVRKYF80Q532
Open the prepared local project file, edit it and explicitly Save. Tabs, search, autosave, recovery and disk conflicts help editing. Opening a folder creates no database copies or File Records.
} r_1Y7YWDKC4AAY8YXVRKYF80Q532

IDE language tools (@language-tools: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-files: 2) { r_6P0TTVZWMFTCA8KZ79CZ8DAERZ
Inspect server, formatter and linter settings and Connect or Disconnect. When installed, try one diagnostic or undoable format on the prepared file. Missing programs do not prevent reading or progression.
} r_6P0TTVZWMFTCA8KZ79CZ8DAERZ

Document Viewer (@documents: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-files: 3) { r_0SXTWM4JHPHHJCMX0W1G296H13
Open the bundled PDF or EPUB sample and move to another page or location. Find its basic reading controls. Reading a document requires no database import.
} r_0SXTWM4JHPHHJCMX0W1G296H13

Terminal (@terminal: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-files: 4) { r_5V2N4Y6C9RZQ024HHE2DH6QD7D
Inspect local shell input and output, or run the harmless practice example. Optional live shell use follows ordinary permissions. Saved Commands are reusable actions; Terminal input belongs to the current session.
} r_5V2N4Y6C9RZQ024HHE2DH6QD7D

Dropping and pasting files (@external-files: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-files: 5) { r_1Z6GJTWH0BS5KAMDYSGX0XAWB9
Use a bundled local sample to inspect file, image and link opening choices and Cancel. Images and links can become Sands; documents and editable files have viewers. Remote downloads are optional.
} r_1Z6GJTWH0BS5KAMDYSGX0XAWB9

Recorder Castle (@recorder: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-creative: 1) { r_3A9DZ8143J7HC908N94WPR8VNS
Play the bundled sample and inspect recordings and track effects. Find Record, Stop, Save and Refresh. Microphone recording is optional; a prepared playback sample needs no capture permission.
} r_3A9DZ8143J7HC908N94WPR8VNS

Sound on Area crossing (@area-sound: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-creative: 2) { r_0JV05HZ991RY3QYJAFNT7361G6
Assign a bundled sound to the sample Area and preview it. Entry and exit use the same boundary crossings as property changes. Saved effects can be reused. Audio hardware does not determine progression.
} r_0JV05HZ991RY3QYJAFNT7361G6

Shader Castle (@shaders: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-creative: 3) { r_00PST668FGREB730ZVV1W5G31S
Inspect the prepared shader effect, such as the glowing ball, and open its Record. The effect is presentation; its authoring text lives with the Record. A shader-language course is optional.
} r_00PST668FGREB730ZVV1W5G31S

Spatial view and Topology (@topology: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-creative: 4) { r_6AQDWY9ACDZQQTF7K9XPZ88HBE
Switch the prepared workspace between 2D and 3D and frame a sample. Depth, rotation and world pinning refine placement. Imported models and splats are optional. Navigation, placement and Areas retain their shared roles.
} r_6AQDWY9ACDZQQTF7K9XPZ88HBE

Custom Castles and the library (@custom-castles: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-creative: 5) { r_7NVY6CKSSTYTH2Z8RR01P4PWJJ
Save a small practice composition and add another instance. Inspect its local file or Organ library entry. Rename, replace, delete and pushing selected composition are further choices. Sharing is optional.
} r_7NVY6CKSSTYTH2Z8RR01P4PWJJ

Freedoom (@freedoom: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-creative: 6) { r_194S1YJ1N9WT0FSZHP4VN8AFY6
Find Start, focus the keyboard controls and locate the way to leave. Reading is enough; playing or completing the game is optional. Sand credits identify bundled software and assets.
} r_194S1YJ1N9WT0FSZHP4VN8AFY6

Inspection (@inspection: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-maintaining: 1) { r_0TJQ9C8GQS6M1EDYH1F3FFG4JQ
Inspect one sample control action, connection or group. Click, hover, events and hidden views offer different perspectives. Inspection helps explain behavior; ordinary work needs no implementation tour.
} r_0TJQ9C8GQS6M1EDYH1F3FFG4JQ

Information, updates and credits (@information: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-maintaining: 2) { r_46VDD6HQG1ERQ6FH8T110F8TYH
Find version, directory and update status, then a Sand license and credits. Read the available update and restart controls. Neither an update nor a restart is required.
} r_46VDD6HQG1ERQ6FH8T110F8TYH

Laboratory (@laboratory: 0, #instinct, #part-of @instinct-maintaining: 3) { r_4W8FGVW9F1FNADEQS73JDHNHNZ
Laboratory runs checks with temporary data and normal workspaces suspended. Open it, inspect a prepared behavior or resource result and Close. Stop ends a run. Performance and stress work are optional maintenance tools.
} r_4W8FGVW9F1FNADEQS73JDHNHNZ

Open editing (@step-interface-open-edit: 0, #instinct, #part-of @sands) { r_5S865TZMJ8DVYXZSA1ESGNF8QA
Open Edit mode in the practice workspace. Next opens the same editing panel.
} r_5S865TZMJ8DVYXZSA1ESGNF8QA

Place ordinary Sands (@step-interface-place-sand: 0, #instinct, #part-of @sands) { r_4VHSSQWR6EGRX4QYE23TBSSKXP
Add an empty Square and plain text Sand. Move and resize the sample. Next places the prepared pair using ordinary placement.
} r_4VHSSQWR6EGRX4QYE23TBSSKXP

Compose a Castle (@step-interface-compose-castle: 0, #instinct, #part-of @castles) { r_2495W3SXVZXTNGXE307TDWW99P
Select the prepared pieces, group them and choose an enclosing row arrangement. Next applies that composition. Try ungrouping when you want independent pieces.
} r_2495W3SXVZXTNGXE307TDWW99P

Place an Area (@step-area-place: 0, #instinct, #part-of @areas-of-influence) { r_4AEKSTE9J0QVXE28AJKD5BYKC1
Place a square Area around the ordinary practice Sand. Compare shape and reach and turn it off and on. Next places the sample Area; no Protein is involved.
} r_4AEKSTE9J0QVXE28AJKD5BYKC1

Observe attraction (@step-area-attract: 0, #instinct, #part-of @areas-of-influence) { r_1FRCBZWACYMC2X175R4SDD11EW
Enable practice workspace physics and sample Area attraction. Wait for movement toward its target. Next applies the settings and waits for the resulting force.
} r_1FRCBZWACYMC2X175R4SDD11EW

Observe repulsion (@step-area-repel: 0, #instinct, #part-of @areas-of-influence) { r_6A86XX56DS4YVTMZVW818SYG76
Switch the sample Area to repulsion. Next changes the same force setting and waits for a force away from the target.
} r_6A86XX56DS4YVTMZVW818SYG76

Create a Protein Spawn Area (@step-protein-create-spawn-area: 0, #instinct, #part-of @protein) { r_3NCZK47MFXCW0FGQCFZXKZRBF0
Create an Area and make it a Protein Spawn Area, using the prepared practice Cell. Next creates the same view through ordinary interface actions.
} r_3NCZK47MFXCW0FGQCFZXKZRBF0

Filter and preview (@step-protein-filter-preview: 0, #instinct, #part-of @protein) { r_1HXFFNF0GKHHBN88EBGTZXYFMG
Filter the prepared data to sample Records and inspect results before spawning. Next applies the filter and waits for the expected sample identities.
} r_1HXFFNF0GKHHBN88EBGTZXYFMG

Present properties (@step-protein-present-properties: 0, #instinct, #part-of @protein) { r_4JJ3TY0H1S81FBQD1X8H0CAQKP
Choose Title and Quantity in the row template. Next applies those presentation choices and waits for both sample Records. Their saved meaning stays the same.
} r_4JJ3TY0H1S81FBQD1X8H0CAQKP

Match the sample (@step-area-match-record: 0, #instinct, #part-of @area-record-actions) { r_6ZZ9NTMX8AX9DCWY466T8F397E
Match only the first prepared Record. Set entry Quantity 1 and exit Quantity 0 while it is outside. Next prepares this isolated example and enables changes.
} r_6ZZ9NTMX8AX9DCWY466T8F397E

Confirm entry (@step-area-change-on-entry: 0, #instinct, #part-of @area-record-actions) { r_4X7FGT5NXT0BJCC50HCSKENK1S
Move the first sample Sand inside and wait for confirmed Quantity 1. Next performs the ordinary movement and waits for the saved change.
} r_4X7FGT5NXT0BJCC50HCSKENK1S

Confirm exit (@step-area-change-on-exit: 0, #instinct, #part-of @area-record-actions) { r_0ZE4PFTHBX5X8WGHGPE9VDDZ2G
Move the same sample outside and wait for confirmed Quantity 0. Next performs the exit movement and waits for confirmation.
} r_0ZE4PFTHBX5X8WGHGPE9VDDZ2G

Workspaces create (@step-workspaces-create: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @workspaces: 1) { r_1FGY7Z0JP7XP0YP2GBXW7KB1D1
    """Create a workspace called Instinct example. Switch away and return to the practice scene. It contains a layout, while an Organ chooses whose data you use."""
} r_1FGY7Z0JP7XP0YP2GBXW7KB1D1

Canvas frame (@step-canvas-frame: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @canvas: 1) { r_6Q6EXAN0KBDJGW69FXYQT7BWNK
    """Place two sample Sands, zoom out, and bring the view back to the centre. Panning and zooming change your view; they do not change the Records."""
} r_6Q6EXAN0KBDJGW69FXYQT7BWNK

Edit mode open (@step-edit-mode-open: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @edit-mode: 1) { r_615PGQWZTHRPFFEZ9J0BF7ZQT8
    """Open Edit mode. Find the store and the workspace controls. You can close editing when you want to use the tools."""
} r_615PGQWZTHRPFFEZ9J0BF7ZQT8

Text sands edit (@step-text-sands-edit: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @text-sands: 1) { r_56F3ZM8XYYN7DE7FEWHRXZFMJB
    """Change the sample label to My practice note. Add an editable note and write Today I tried Lince. The note is part of this practice layout."""
} r_56F3ZM8XYYN7DE7FEWHRXZFMJB

Appearance change (@step-appearance-change: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @appearance: 1) { r_4EH1XBJPMAS58RJSGQY4PJHDR7
    """Give the sample Square a different paper colour. This change belongs to the sample, so other Squares keep their own appearance."""
} r_4EH1XBJPMAS58RJSGQY4PJHDR7

Appearance reset (@step-appearance-reset: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @appearance: 2) { r_66QFSCE7V1WTWX602KATMGVCQ1
    """Reset the sample colour to its inherited theme. A reset removes an override; it does not replace the theme."""
} r_66QFSCE7V1WTWX602KATMGVCQ1

Shortcuts inspect (@step-shortcuts-inspect: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @shortcuts: 1) { r_0XMZQBR943PJQVNTCCCW5CXZB3
    """Open the shortcut settings. Move focus with Tab and activate a practice button with the keyboard. Ctrl Shift Escape always discards this practice, even after shortcut remapping."""
} r_0XMZQBR943PJQVNTCCCW5CXZB3

Area effects scale (@step-area-effects-scale: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @area-effects: 1) { r_55DKBXB6YM1DHGGH6GDH5BBSA9
    """Put an ordinary sample Sand inside the Area and set its size effect to one and a half. Compare the affected sample with a Sand outside."""
} r_55DKBXB6YM1DHGGH6GDH5BBSA9

Area effects disable (@step-area-effects-disable: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @area-effects: 2) { r_1B85RANDFDA9JANQY9BFMMHVZD
    """Return the size effect to one. Turn the Area off and inspect the ordinary sample again. No Record quantity or Assertion changes here."""
} r_1B85RANDFDA9JANQY9BFMMHVZD

Area inspection inspect (@step-area-inspection-inspect: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @area-inspection: 1) { r_783JC83YMQN9ZDKBM52FJMJTYC
    """Open the sample Area and its influence explanation. Read its enabled state, reach and effect on the sample. If a Sand is pinned or immune, the explanation tells you why it is excluded."""
} r_783JC83YMQN9ZDKBM52FJMJTYC

Learn record sample (@step-learn-record-sample: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @learn-record: 1) { r_78Q4EZEZZR4VG2HARJEW4J63CS
    """Create an isolated sample note with a title, body and slug, and give it a Need of one. Open its full Record view. This practice uses a separate Cell; it cannot edit your personal Records."""
} r_78Q4EZEZZR4VG2HARJEW4J63CS

Learn assertion sample (@step-learn-assertion-sample: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @learn-assertion: 1) { r_1JETEP3V4ZJXQK3TDKXQWWQCHB
    """Add the concept practice-note and a relation to a second sample Record. Choose practice-note as the main identity. Inspect the saved Assertions on the sample."""
} r_1JETEP3V4ZJXQK3TDKXQWWQCHB

Learn ontology inspect (@step-learn-ontology-inspect: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @learn-ontology: 1) { r_0J8Q1MBH0Q8B5NADT06W0RFPQ8
    """Look at the sample concept practice-note in the local Vocabulary. The hierarchy and alias help explain its meaning. These sample concepts live in the isolated Cell."""
} r_0J8Q1MBH0Q8B5NADT06W0RFPQ8

Record castles open (@step-record-castles-open: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @record-castles: 1) { r_0D77DDANKJ9TKZN4CYA20B4YWX
    """Open the full Record and its Assertion view for the same isolated note. Follow its relation to the second sample. The views share data; changing the view does not create another Record."""
} r_0D77DDANKJ9TKZN4CYA20B4YWX

Facts inspect (@step-facts-inspect: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @facts: 1) { r_55KJNH2K3SCZ79VPJDJGPJCKY7
    """Inspect the confirmed quantity change on the sample and its time. A Fact records what changed, not just what someone planned to change."""
} r_55KJNH2K3SCZ79VPJDJGPJCKY7

Protein arrangement arrange (@step-protein-arrangement-arrange: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @protein-arrangement: 1) { r_0MS7HDNZCKMDVDFGKEENYG3GRY
    """Arrange the two prepared Protein results vertically and show their titles and quantities. This changes the layout of the live results while preserving the Records."""
} r_0MS7HDNZCKMDVDFGKEENYG3GRY

Complete a sample task (@step-todo-complete: 0, #instinct, #part-of @todo: 1) { r_3X88FAM6CZN3CFEGG1HP1GMX9E
    """The prepared task has quantity -1: it is a Need. Complete it and wait for the saved quantity to reach zero. The Todo queue contains live data; finishing its presentation changes the same Record shown in the Record view."""
} r_3X88FAM6CZN3CFEGG1HP1GMX9E

Undo the sample completion (@step-todo-undo: 0, #instinct, #part-of @todo: 2) { r_3BZH4N1Y7PZE6WTGG4GD43JHE0
    """Undo the sample completion. Confirm that its quantity returns to -1 and the task appears in the live queue again. Undo applies a new saved change, so its history remains truthful."""
} r_3BZH4N1Y7PZE6WTGG4GD43JHE0

Move the sample to Next (@step-kanban-move: 0, #instinct, #part-of @kanban: 1) { r_1VZVK6WXE24PSXY8NVZPCWJX7C
    """Move the prepared task from Todo to Next. These columns are Areas: entering a column applies its state to the same task. Inspect the resulting quantity and Assertion, then compare the column count with the Record view."""
} r_1VZVK6WXE24PSXY8NVZPCWJX7C

Start a sample stopwatch (@step-time-start: 0, #instinct, #part-of @time: 1) { r_774SP40KVAH6E3PDJC0JNY6M6T
    """Start the standalone practice stopwatch. It measures time in this workspace. A timer attached to a Record instead saves a work log with that Record; choose the kind that fits the work you are tracking."""
} r_774SP40KVAH6E3PDJC0JNY6M6T

Stop and inspect the stopwatch (@step-time-stop: 0, #instinct, #part-of @time: 2) { r_2PZVMGS337ZVBFS1XCAWYQVDW5
    """Stop the sample stopwatch and inspect its completed interval. A completed interval stays in the log. You can start another interval without replacing the previous one."""
} r_2PZVMGS337ZVBFS1XCAWYQVDW5

Open a dated sample (@step-calendar-open: 0, #instinct, #part-of @calendar: 1) { r_7NMD2G788XQK2V37AQCPVW0B3A
    """The prepared note has a start date and a due date. Find its date in the Calendar and open the same note in the Record view. Scheduled and projected changes identify their sources; Frequency and Karma explain those sources in the next chapter."""
} r_7NMD2G788XQK2V37AQCPVW0B3A

Activate a sample operation (@step-operation-activate: 0, #instinct, #part-of @operation: 1) { r_4420FDZ73VRMJ7PR8H0Y5CZRZF
    """Activate the sample operation to set the prepared note's quantity to zero. Wait for the Cell to confirm the change. An Operation provides a short action; saved Commands and their execution history are introduced separately."""
} r_4420FDZ73VRMJ7PR8H0Y5CZRZF

Inspect sample feedback (@step-notifications-open: 0, #instinct, #part-of @notifications: 1) { r_414YN9RKG0GQXXYSS6PEW730DB
    """Open the sample notification. It reports a completed practice action. Waiting, success and failure feedback tell you whether a request was received or confirmed; a system notification is optional."""
} r_414YN9RKG0GQXXYSS6PEW730DB

Dismiss sample feedback (@step-notifications-dismiss: 0, #instinct, #part-of @notifications: 2) { r_74Z42F9Q06ZHPX3TNPJKV35G1N
    """Dismiss only the sample notification. Dismissing feedback removes it from the visible list; it does not undo the saved action that it described."""
} r_74Z42F9Q06ZHPX3TNPJKV35G1N

Move, resize and pin a sample (@step-interface-move-sand: 0, is #idea, #instinct, #part-of @sands: 3) { r_24N8JXSY7PAAX0RSMFV8A2B88A
